WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.392 --> 00:00:02.475
(swoosh)

00:00:03.441 --> 00:00:06.024
(upbeat music)

00:00:13.056 --> 00:00:15.910
- Talk to us, Evan, please
a little bit about the book,

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:19.481
Your One Word, how did
that idea come to fruition?

00:00:19.481 --> 00:00:21.828
Like was it something you'd
been planning all along

00:00:21.828 --> 00:00:23.951
or were you just one day like
I'm going to write a book,

00:00:23.951 --> 00:00:25.664
let's make this happen?

00:00:25.664 --> 00:00:27.206
- I never wanted to write a book.

00:00:27.206 --> 00:00:28.759
It wasn't my thing.

00:00:28.759 --> 00:00:30.826
My agent Steve in New York

00:00:30.826 --> 00:00:32.402
is like we need a book, you need a book.

00:00:32.402 --> 00:00:34.805
I need a book to sell
you into corporations

00:00:34.805 --> 00:00:35.642
and all this stuff.

00:00:35.642 --> 00:00:36.772
Like, I don't want a book, Steve.

00:00:36.772 --> 00:00:38.413
Look at my YouTube channel.

00:00:38.413 --> 00:00:39.905
I can open up doors.

00:00:39.905 --> 00:00:42.438
It's not 1950 anymore, right?

00:00:42.438 --> 00:00:44.294
Like you don't need a
book to open up doors.

00:00:44.294 --> 00:00:45.952
- Yes, sir.

00:00:45.952 --> 00:00:46.785
- I mean, he's like okay,

00:00:46.785 --> 00:00:48.244
I'm going to pitch you
anyway into publishers.

00:00:48.244 --> 00:00:50.804
I'm like, do whatever,
pitch me, it doesn't matter.

00:00:50.804 --> 00:00:53.326
And then through that process

00:00:53.326 --> 00:00:56.501
I was figuring out my one word, believe.

00:00:56.501 --> 00:00:59.023
I started branding my
business around believe.

00:00:59.023 --> 00:01:00.614
My website was about believe.

00:01:00.614 --> 00:01:01.633
My newsletters were about believe.

00:01:01.633 --> 00:01:03.293
I was making videos about believe.

00:01:03.293 --> 00:01:05.355
Everything that was believe related

00:01:05.355 --> 00:01:08.197
took off way more than anything else.

00:01:08.197 --> 00:01:11.441
And so, and one because it's
easy to understand and market

00:01:11.441 --> 00:01:14.401
but two, it was like, it was more me.

00:01:14.401 --> 00:01:15.772
Believe is not just a marketing thing.

00:01:15.772 --> 00:01:16.846
It's authentic for me.

00:01:16.846 --> 00:01:19.623
It's what I am.

00:01:19.623 --> 00:01:22.054
And so, it's curious to
then find other businesses.

00:01:22.054 --> 00:01:23.377
Like I'm going to do this crazy thing

00:01:23.377 --> 00:01:25.699
and build my entire
business around one word.

00:01:25.699 --> 00:01:28.032
It sounds nuts.

00:01:28.032 --> 00:01:31.367
And then I started finding other
businesses that had done it

00:01:31.367 --> 00:01:33.208
and from the guy who just built

00:01:33.208 --> 00:01:35.358
a $50,000 full-time income for himself

00:01:35.358 --> 00:01:37.599
around one word, to then a business

00:01:37.599 --> 00:01:39.961
that had half a million
dollars, a million dollars,

00:01:39.961 --> 00:01:42.842
five million dollars, and 150
million dollars in revenue.

00:01:42.842 --> 00:01:44.380
And I went out to interview these people

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:47.355
and they all just figured it out.

00:01:47.355 --> 00:01:48.393
Nobody had a blueprint.

00:01:48.393 --> 00:01:49.505
There was no plan,

00:01:49.505 --> 00:01:51.195
and so I thought it would be pretty cool

00:01:51.195 --> 00:01:52.028
if there was a plan.

00:01:52.028 --> 00:01:53.354
Like if there's a book
that I want to write,

00:01:53.354 --> 00:01:55.124
that's the book I want to write,

00:01:55.124 --> 00:01:58.260
not this other stuff that
you guys are pitching me.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:00.223
And so, I was really
reluctant at the start.

00:02:00.223 --> 00:02:01.717
I like didn't want to do it at all

00:02:01.717 --> 00:02:05.215
and I was just following my agent,

00:02:05.215 --> 00:02:06.694
and like didn't want to take calls,

00:02:06.694 --> 00:02:07.690
and didn't want to do like,

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:09.294
we'd take a call and
then give us a propose.

00:02:09.294 --> 00:02:10.384
I'm like a don't want to do a proposal.

00:02:10.384 --> 00:02:11.848
I don't even want to do a book.

00:02:11.848 --> 00:02:12.932
But then when this idea came,

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:16.026
I'm like guys, this is
it, this is the thing.

00:02:16.026 --> 00:02:18.130
And they hated it at the start.

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:19.530
They're like, that's a workbook,

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:22.066
that's like five pages of a worksheet.

00:02:22.066 --> 00:02:23.017
Like, are you kidding me?

00:02:23.017 --> 00:02:24.721
This is more than a book,

00:02:24.721 --> 00:02:26.373
this is a series.

00:02:26.373 --> 00:02:29.872
And they're like for a book
they want like 60,000 words.

00:02:29.872 --> 00:02:32.099
That's how much like a
typical book is going to be.

00:02:32.099 --> 00:02:34.776
I wrote 120,000 words.

00:02:34.776 --> 00:02:36.556
- Oh God.

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:38.289
- We cut half the book.

00:02:38.289 --> 00:02:40.242
We cut an entire book,

00:02:40.242 --> 00:02:42.927
and they're like oh, we
can use that as volume two.

00:02:42.927 --> 00:02:44.125
I'm like no, no, no, I'm like,

00:02:44.125 --> 00:02:45.867
we're not even keeping it,
I'm throwing that away.

00:02:45.867 --> 00:02:46.969
Like, if I write another book,

00:02:46.969 --> 00:02:47.932
it'll be something different.

00:02:47.932 --> 00:02:50.347
It's like just grind out the work

00:02:50.347 --> 00:02:52.485
and I'll throw away more
than what most people

00:02:52.485 --> 00:02:53.318
will even create

00:02:53.318 --> 00:02:56.334
and so, like that's the
best of the 120,000 words

00:02:56.334 --> 00:03:00.067
condensed down to 60 or
65 or whatever it is.

00:03:00.067 --> 00:03:02.591
I just got really excited
about being able to teach

00:03:02.591 --> 00:03:03.644
the concept and I thought

00:03:03.644 --> 00:03:06.770
it would actually lend
itself better to a book

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:08.523
because of the activities and exercises,

00:03:08.523 --> 00:03:10.350
than making YouTube videos.

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:11.615
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:03:11.615 --> 00:03:13.904
Thank you to the guys from VNR Media

00:03:13.904 --> 00:03:15.232
for the awesome interview.

00:03:15.232 --> 00:03:16.885
The full link is in the description below

00:03:16.885 --> 00:03:18.019
if you want to check it out.

00:03:18.019 --> 00:03:19.974
I'd love to know what did you think?

00:03:19.974 --> 00:03:21.121
What are your thoughts?

00:03:21.121 --> 00:03:22.765
